# Single-page-app fallback.
#
# The app is client-routed (React Router), so paths like /learning/run-001 or
# /settings/delete-account exist only in the browser. A static host that doesn't
# know that returns its own 404 on a refresh or a shared deep link — which is
# exactly the class of bug that appears only in production.
#
# Honoured by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages, which serve a real file if one exists
# and only fall through to this rule otherwise. Other hosts need the equivalent:
#   Vercel          → "rewrites": [{ "source": "/(.*)", "destination": "/index.html" }]
#   Firebase        → "rewrites": [{ "source": "**", "destination": "/index.html" }]
#   GitHub Pages    → copy index.html to 404.html as part of the build
#
# See CUTOVER.md §6.
/*    /index.html   200
